  "title": "Queen Seondeok of Silla",
  "summary": "Seondeok ruled the Korean kingdom of Silla from 632 to 647 and is described as the first female sovereign of ancient Korea. She succeeded her father Jinpyeong, who had no male heir. The Cheomseongdae observatory in Gyeongju dates to her reign.",
